# Force LF on checkout everywhere, including Windows.
#
# Without this, git's autocrlf converts checked-out files to CRLF on Windows.
# That silently breaks anything that reads source as text: a regex ending
# `` `\n `` stops matching (`DEFAULT_RULES_YAML not found`), string equality
# against rule actions yields `'block\r'`, and line counts drift.
#
# keel reads its own source in several tests (the shipped default rules are
# extracted from plugin.ts), so CRLF is a correctness problem here, not a
# cosmetic one.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Genuinely binary — never touch these.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
